  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MVI-Mekong Climate Resilience</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MVi is one of IP1 and IP2 partners actively working in Steung Treng province where the hydropower dam in the mainstream has been planned. MVI has supported riverine community to document the ecological change and impacts of water changes using fish catchmonitoring where feminist participatory action research methods are applied. MVI is also building IPs women river defenders and engaging themwith various network for voicing.
MVI realized human-made and climate disaster are the issues of riverine communities it works with. MVI identified climate change is one of strategic priorities of its organization. MVI has successful experiences of implementing climate change adaptation and mitigation project with UNDP and Forum CIV. For instance, MVi supported three communities in Steung Treng to build small scale dam for improving capacity of community adaption activities. MVI supported strengthen capacity of community and local authorities to jointly project forestry from illegal logging and increasing forest cover.
MVI is a member of Cambodia Humanitarian Forum (CHF), a national network on disaster and humanitarian response. MVI has currently well collaborated with local administrations where the governor of the province or district administrations and chief of commune council are the chairs of provincial,district or commune disaster management committee.
Engaging in the Mekong Climate Resilience Project, provide a chance for MVI to build the capacity of commune and district disaster management committee toconduct vulnerability risk assessment (VRA) to define the hazard risks and develop an inclusive contingency plan for the implementation. In addition, MVi will play crucial role in raising awareness on water data utilization to targeted community and in collaboration with Royal University of Agriculture (RUA) to introduceclimate sensitive livelihoods initiatives or climate smart agriculture model that would help riverine community in the Mekong to adapt to climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">My Village (MVi) was founded in November 2006 and officially registered with the Ministry of Interior in 25 January 2007. Ever since, MVi became a recognized local NGO working for Indigenous Peoples&apos; Rights and Natural Resources Management. MVi encourages ownership and participation of Indigenous Peoples# as its approaches to protect their land and natural resources.
MVi is operating in Northeast provinces of Cambodia, in particular in Mondulkiri, Kratie and Stung Treng, and focused on organizing community forests, helping indigenous people learn about their rights, helping women become empowered, and facilitating communities in undertaking various development projects.
MVi has been worked in collaboration with Community Networks, Provincial and National NGO networks, and line of government institutions at the national and provincial level of Department of Local Administrative of Ministry of Interior, Department of Forestry Administrative, Department of Agriculture, Department of Environment, Department of Land Use Management, and Department of Rural Development.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">My Village Organization</narrative>
